Subject: One dash budget per canvas, counting flattened curve segments

0012 gave each dashed traversal a budget of one million dash segments,
but two things escaped it, both found by zusvg's fuzzer. Flattening a
cubic subdivides to a depth of 31 in user units, so one curve hundreds of
millions of units long became 37 million line segments before a single
dash was cut, and none of them was counted. And the budget was per path,
so every <use> of a dashed path, or every dashed path in a document,
brought a million more.

Keep the budget in plutovg_canvas_t, so that every stroke made on one
canvas shares PLUTOVG_MAX_DASH_SEGMENTS (one million), and charge
flattened segments to it as well as dashes. When it is spent, a curve
being flattened is finished with straight segments to its pending end
points, and later strokes are drawn solid without dashing, their curves
left to the FreeType stroker. plutovg_path_traverse_dashed() and
plutovg_path_clone_dashed() keep one budget per call; the internal
plutovg_path_clone_dashed_budget() takes the canvas's.

zusvg: .agents/design.md §12, D18; issue #27. Offered upstream.

